 "text": "9/30/26, 5:12 AM\nIn Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable, you create business partners with customer or vendor master records manually. On\nthe SAP Easy Access screen, choose |sAccounting Financial Accounting \u00bb Contract Accounts Receivable and Payable \u00bb Master\nData Business Partner  Customer/Customer Integration } Create Business Partner with Customer 9 and |\u00bbSupplier/ Vendor\n\nIntegration \u00bb Create Business Partner with Vendor .. There you can also access transactions for changing and displaying master\ndata. These transactions use role groupings that already contain the necessary roles for synchronous creation of\n\ncustomers/customers and suppliers/vendors. This ensures that the system creates the business partner in the role MKK, and that\nyou can enter information on the company code and sales (or the company code and purchasing) using the roles FLCU00 and\nFLCUOQ1 or FLVNOO and FLVNO1.\n\nPrerequisites\n\ne You are familiar with the basic settings of the master data objects business partner, customer, and vendor.\n\ne You have experience with configuring the data exchange using CRM middleware \u2014 assuming that SAP CRM is part of your\n\nscenario.\n\ne During the synchronization and replication, both the S/AHANA system and the CRM system are available - assuming CRM\nis part of your scenario.\n\n1 Note\n\nFor more information, see the following SAP Notes:\n\nSAP Note         Description\n852870 Phe         BP_CVI: Changes in BDT Customizing for ERP 2005\n\n905535 Phe       Useful Notes \u2014 CVI for Master Data Synchronization\n\n928616 Php        BP_CVI: Customizing of Required Entry Fields for BP/Customer\n\n941955 Phe        BP_CVI: Integration of Customers/Vendors with SAP BP\n\n954816 Phe         BP_CVI: Transactions for Creating/Linking BPs\n\n956054 Pie        BP_CVI Customer / Vendor Integration as of ERP2005 (ECC600)\n\n1968132 Phe       Business Partner Replication Between CRM and ECC with Active CVI\n\nActivities\n\nIf you are using the integration between SAP CRM and SAP S/HANA, then you have to make the settings described in all of the\nfollowing topics. If you are using only SAP S/4HANA, then only make the settings described in the following two topics:\n\ne Making Settings for Customer/Vendor Integration\n\ne Making Settings for the Postprocessing Office\n\nThe synchronization and replication of master data between SAP CRM and SAP S/4HANA requires extensive settings:\n\ne For the SAP business partner in the S/4AHANA system and CRM system\n\n-\u2014 Cartan (DAA midndlavsarn in than C /ALIANIA evrctam and (DAA evietanm\n",
